<h2>Project overview</h2>
<!-- PLACEHOLDER -->
<div class="ph">
  <p>Okiro is an atmospheric adventure set in the space between dreaming and waking. Players drift through shifting dreamscapes, each one pulling them a little closer to the surface.</p>
  <p>The audio blurs the edges: sounds from the waking world leak into the dream, growing louder as the player nears the end.</p>
</div>

<h2>My role</h2>
<!-- PLACEHOLDER -->
<div class="ph">
  <ul>
    <li>Sound designer: ambiences, transitions and environmental sound</li>
    <li>Audio implementation in Wwise and Unreal Engine</li>
    <li>Field recording: [forests, trains, a ticking clock]</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h2>Technical approach</h2>
<!-- PLACEHOLDER -->
<div class="ph">
  <p>Each dreamscape is a Wwise state with its own blend of ambience layers. A <i>wakefulness</i> RTPC drives filters and sends, so real-world sounds (an alarm clock, traffic, a voice calling the player's name) slowly cut through the dream mix.</p>
  <p>Transitions between areas use spatialised one-shots and a shared reverb bus, so the player never hears a hard cut.</p>
</div>

